  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Last summer \\(30 \\%\\) of the birds living on Town Lake were geese, \\(25 \\%\\) were swans, \\(10 \\%\\) were herons, and \\(35 \\%\\) were ducks. What percent of the birds that were not swans were geese?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(20\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(30\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(40\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(50\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(60\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "40"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2011-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "WLOG, let there be \\(100\\) birds. Then \\(75\\) birds are not swans. The desired percentage is then \\[ \\dfrac{30}{75} \\cdot 100 = 40 \\%. \\]\n\nThus, C is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the percent that are not swans as the denominator",
        "The desired percent is \\(\\frac{30}{100-25}\\)"
      ],
